# Staged by fisher-5sg.3 on 2026-11-24.
# Sources: April 2006 UCI specification https://backscattering.de/chess/uci/,
# fisher-8ie session rules, and fisher-r6y D9–D11, D15, D20, D24, D25 and D28.
# Full searched info: D41 and Stockfish sf_19 (edb0d9d), 2026-11-24.
# See UCIEngine::on_update_full and SearchManager::output_pv.
# Shakmaty 0.30.3 reference minimax, 2026-11-24, confirms the
# python-chess 1.11.2 enumeration on fisher-5sg.13.
# Per-ply nodes: 1/21/30/730 and 1/25/45/1228. At depths 1 and 2
# the horizon sees a queen deficit (cp -900). At depths 3 and 4 both
# searches see mate -1. The only legal moves are h8g8 and h8h7.
# Totals add work from all finished depths of this go (fisher-5sg decision 10).
# fisher-4yn.1, 2026-11-25: a node total at depth 2 or more reads {nodes},
# except below a root with one legal move. Once the search makes cutoffs,
# such a total depends on the order Position::legal_moves returns moves in,
# which nobody chose (fisher-4yn, D36 and D38). A root with one legal move
# puts no bound on the replies, so depth 2 there plays every one and its
# total stays exact (owner decision on PR #74). Scores, depths, principal
# variations, bestmove and the depth-1 totals (the number of legal moves at
# the root) stay exact. A node count in these comments describes the search
# without cutoffs before it.
> position fen 7k/8/5K1Q/8/8/8/8/8 b - - 0 1
# The nonnumeric depth leaves infinite in force (fisher-5sg).
> go depth infinite
< info depth 1 multipv 1 score cp -900 nodes 1 nps {nps} time {time} pv {pv}
< info depth 2 multipv 1 score cp -900 nodes 23 nps {nps} time {time} pv {pv}
> isready
<* info depth {depth} multipv 1 score {score} nodes {nodes} nps {nps} time {time} pv {pv}
< readyok
> stop
<* info depth {depth} multipv 1 score {score} nodes {nodes} nps {nps} time {time} pv {pv}
< bestmove h8g8
# No further output from the stopped search may precede readyok.
> isready
< readyok

# Unknown words before a command are skipped under UCI.
> unknown go infinite
< info depth 1 multipv 1 score cp -900 nodes 1 nps {nps} time {time} pv {pv}
< info depth 2 multipv 1 score cp -900 nodes 23 nps {nps} time {time} pv {pv}
> isready
<* info depth {depth} multipv 1 score {score} nodes {nodes} nps {nps} time {time} pv {pv}
< readyok
# Rule 8 rejects both commands and keeps the original position.
> go
<* info depth {depth} multipv 1 score {score} nodes {nodes} nps {nps} time {time} pv {pv}
< info string {message:go rejected: waiting for stop}
# The ignored command consumes its stop argument.
> setoption name Path value stop
> position fen 7k/8/5K2/6Q1/8/8/8/8 b - - 0 1
<* info depth {depth} multipv 1 score {score} nodes {nodes} nps {nps} time {time} pv {pv}
< info string {message:position rejected: waiting for stop}
> unknown stop
<* info depth {depth} multipv 1 score {score} nodes {nodes} nps {nps} time {time} pv {pv}
< bestmove h8g8
# No further output from the stopped search may precede readyok.
> isready
< readyok

> go
# Rules 4, 5, 7 and 10. See the header for the per-ply counts.
# Rules 2 and 3 score the horizon by material, so depths before the mate show material.
< info depth 1 multipv 1 score cp -900 nodes 1 nps {nps} time {time} pv {pv}
< info depth 2 multipv 1 score cp -900 nodes 23 nps {nps} time {time} pv {pv}
< info depth 3 multipv 1 score mate -1 nodes {nodes} nps {nps} time {time} pv {pv}
< info depth 4 multipv 1 score mate -1 nodes {nodes} nps {nps} time {time} pv {pv}
# The owner keeps the original position, whose only legal move is h8g8.
< bestmove h8g8
> go
# Rules 4, 5, 7 and 10. See the header for the per-ply counts.
# Rules 2 and 3 score the horizon by material, so depths before the mate show material.
< info depth 1 multipv 1 score cp -900 nodes 1 nps {nps} time {time} pv {pv}
< info depth 2 multipv 1 score cp -900 nodes 23 nps {nps} time {time} pv {pv}
< info depth 3 multipv 1 score mate -1 nodes {nodes} nps {nps} time {time} pv {pv}
< info depth 4 multipv 1 score mate -1 nodes {nodes} nps {nps} time {time} pv {pv}
# The reference also kept the original position.
< bestmove {legal}
# The prefixed stop allows the engine and reference to follow the next position.
> position fen 7k/8/5K2/6Q1/8/8/8/8 b - - 0 1
> go
# Rules 4, 5, 7 and 10. See the header for the per-ply counts.
# Rules 2 and 3 score the horizon by material, so depths before the mate show material.
< info depth 1 multipv 1 score cp -900 nodes 1 nps {nps} time {time} pv {pv}
< info depth 2 multipv 1 score cp -900 nodes 27 nps {nps} time {time} pv {pv}
< info depth 3 multipv 1 score mate -1 nodes {nodes} nps {nps} time {time} pv {pv}
< info depth 4 multipv 1 score mate -1 nodes {nodes} nps {nps} time {time} pv {pv}
# Black's only legal move in the replacement position is h8h7.
< bestmove h8h7
> go
# Rules 4, 5, 7 and 10. See the header for the per-ply counts.
# Rules 2 and 3 score the horizon by material, so depths before the mate show material.
< info depth 1 multipv 1 score cp -900 nodes 1 nps {nps} time {time} pv {pv}
< info depth 2 multipv 1 score cp -900 nodes 27 nps {nps} time {time} pv {pv}
< info depth 3 multipv 1 score mate -1 nodes {nodes} nps {nps} time {time} pv {pv}
< info depth 4 multipv 1 score mate -1 nodes {nodes} nps {nps} time {time} pv {pv}
< bestmove {legal}
> stop
> isready
# UCI ignores an idle stop and replies to isready.
< readyok
# UCI quit.
> quit
! exit
